<%# Stop Alpine's generated DOM from being cached by Turbo and then rendered a
    SECOND time on the way back.

    The bug, as the operator hit it: make 6 of 6 picks, follow the wallet
    modal's "Read the setup guide" link, press Back — and "Your Picks" shows
    TWELVE rows, the six real picks plus six blanks.

    The mechanism is a seam between two libraries that are each behaving
    correctly. Turbo snapshots the LIVE DOM, which by then contains the elements
    Alpine's `x-for` GENERATED, and a restoration visit puts that snapshot back
    verbatim. Alpine then initialises the restored tree from scratch: its
    `x-for` keeps its bookkeeping (`_x_lookup`) on the template element as a JS
    property, and JS properties do not survive the snapshot — so the fresh
    `x-for` has no idea the snapshot already carries a full set of rows, and
    renders another one beside it. The cached rows are left with no Alpine
    scope, which is why they render blank rather than as doubled picks.

    Measured on /contests/<slug> before this partial existed: after one Back the
    page carried 12 cart slots instead of 6, and the seeds bar's `x-for i in 5`
    went to 10. So this is not a cart bug — it is every `x-for` and `x-if` on
    any cached page, and the fix belongs here rather than in one partial.

    The cure is to hand Turbo a snapshot that contains only the TEMPLATES, never
    their output. On `turbo:before-cache` we drop the generated nodes and clear
    the bookkeeping that points at them; the restored page then renders exactly
    one set. This mutates the live DOM, which is the same bargain the gear
    sidebar and the engine's modal host already strike on this event — Turbo
    fires it once the visit is committed and the body is about to be replaced.

    x-for is swept BEFORE x-if on purpose: an x-for row can contain x-if
    templates, and removing the row takes its nested templates with it.

    NOT the engine's copy of this problem. studio-engine ships Alpine and every
    app on it has the same seam; this fixes turf-monster, where it was reported.
%>
<script>
  (function () {
    if (window.__turfAlpineTurboCacheReset) return;
    window.__turfAlpineTurboCacheReset = true;

    function resetGeneratedAlpineDom() {
      // x-for: `_x_lookup` is a Map of key -> generated element.
      document.querySelectorAll('template[x-for]').forEach(function (tpl) {
        var lookup = tpl._x_lookup;
        if (lookup && typeof lookup.forEach === 'function') {
          lookup.forEach(function (node) {
            if (node && typeof node.remove === 'function') node.remove();
          });
          if (typeof lookup.clear === 'function') lookup.clear();
        }
        delete tpl._x_lastRenderedEl;
      });

      // x-if: `_x_currentIfEl` is the single element the template inserted.
      document.querySelectorAll('template[x-if]').forEach(function (tpl) {
        var clone = tpl._x_currentIfEl;
        if (clone && typeof clone.remove === 'function') clone.remove();
        delete tpl._x_currentIfEl;
      });
    }

    document.addEventListener('turbo:before-cache', resetGeneratedAlpineDom);
  })();
</script>
